<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1eae9d4612040b449727d73289effd61a1ea493e" commit="4a0ca860ec24a76cfc10e2c949d65eb88b3b9d54" commit_message="UPSTREAM: sched/fair: Fix sched_entity::avg::decay_count initialization  Child has the same decay_count as parent. If it's not zero, we add it to parent's cfs_rq-&gt;removed_load:  wake_up_new_task()-&gt;set_task_cpu()-&gt;migrate_task_rq_fair().  Child's load is a just garbade after copying of parent, it hasn't been on cfs_rq yet, and it must not be added to cfs_rq::removed_load in migrate_task_rq_fair().  The patch moves sched_entity::avg::decay_count intialization in sched_fork(). So, migrate_task_rq_fair() does not change removed_load.  Signed-off-by: Kirill Tkhai &lt;ktkhai@parallels.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Peter Zijlstra (Intel) &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Segall &lt;bsegall@google.com&gt; Cc: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/1418644618.6074.13.camel@tkhai Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit bb04159df99fa353d0fb524574aca03ce2c6515b) Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44828 TEST=Boot kernel on Oak. TEST=smaug-release and strago-release trybots.  Change-Id: I1eae9d4612040b449727d73289effd61a1ea493e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312182 Commit-Ready: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312182" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/82/312182/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib7465b8ea33720e00bf96b75a15e072c90405597" commit="8129e7a3b77b14ccce1fe026d20f5b7bd7b471eb" commit_message="UPSTREAM: sched/fair: Fix a comment reflecting function name change  update_cfs_rq_load_contribution() was changed to __update_cfs_rq_tg_load_contrib() - sync up the commit in calc_tg_weight() too.  Signed-off-by: Byungchul Park &lt;byungchul.park@lge.com&gt; Cc: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Cc: Peter Zijlstra &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/1436187062-19658-1-git-send-email-byungchul.park@lge.com Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 399595f248cb25dccb6044b53c47c44c174dc23d) Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44828 TEST=Boot kernel on Oak. TEST=smaug-release and strago-release trybots.  Change-Id: Ib7465b8ea33720e00bf96b75a15e072c90405597 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312183 Commit-Ready: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312183" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/83/312183/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib03e7ba34b7ab6c5b40d63d4fb931fc5d5d4fa58" commit="58d3cb6d437b29e7196af60f55f1f4220a192790" commit_message="UPSTREAM: sched: Move the loadavg code to a more obvious location  I could not find the loadavg code.. turns out it was hidden in a file called proc.c. It further got mingled up with the cruft per rq load indexes (which we really want to get rid of).  Move the per rq load indexes into the fair.c load-balance code (that's the only thing that uses them) and rename proc.c to loadavg.c so we can find it again.  Signed-off-by: Peter Zijlstra (Intel) &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Borislav Petkov &lt;bp@alien8.de&gt; Cc: H. Peter Anvin &lt;hpa@zytor.com&gt; Cc: Paul Gortmaker &lt;paul.gortmaker@windriver.com&gt; Cc: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; [ Did minor cleanups to the code. ] Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt;  (cherry picked from commit 3289bdb429884c0279bf9ab72dff7b934f19dfc6) Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44828 TEST=Boot kernel on Oak. TEST=smaug-release and strago-release trybots.  Change-Id: Ib03e7ba34b7ab6c5b40d63d4fb931fc5d5d4fa58 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312184 Commit-Ready: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312184" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/84/312184/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib724e2ac1da9a621c6ba0cdcf5a301ddf04a4afb" commit="94e80820e526fe9bc0f44ccee6c576c47a85eb61" commit_message="cros-kernel2: Set CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC_32BIT=n  The 32-bit API is old (Android &lt;=4.4), and the config option is ignored on 64-bit architectures anyway, let's set the default to =n.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:*246015 BUG=b:26735760 TEST=N/A  Change-Id: Ib724e2ac1da9a621c6ba0cdcf5a301ddf04a4afb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323626 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Hansen &lt;benhansen@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="323626" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/26/323626/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I145d4c85755f0b885bcf7e59b7284c2a60993303" commit="b5637afb4f1ce767a652414a2ea07219c61fd645" commit_message="skylake boards: prepare for separate verstage  In order for the skylake boards to have a separate verstage and run romstage from the RW slots one has to ensure the FSP and romstage are added to CBFS for XIP (execute-in-place). This requires one to re-add FSP and romstage so that the two files are relocated. Additionally, remove verstage from the RW slots since verstage would never be run from the RW slots.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=glados TEST=Built and booted chell using separate verstage. Also, suspended      and resumed.  Change-Id: I145d4c85755f0b885bcf7e59b7284c2a60993303 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323421 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323421" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/21/323421/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I36350f708dd25ca3c8852aead5ab5ff940b71e9a" commit="ad116da8b6d1a72adf194656b907660d41dca942" commit_message="gooftool: add '-r BOOT_STUB' when running cbfstool  We need to add additional '-r BOOT_STUB' to get locale information when using cbfstool.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48407 TEST=     1. vpd -i RO_VPD -s locale=us     2. run finalize  Change-Id: I36350f708dd25ca3c8852aead5ab5ff940b71e9a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323902 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: JAMES C Chen &lt;james.c.chen@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323902" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/02/323902/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic20be2024afedabc2d8bc767f1b794376348523c" commit="8d557702e74438cf1032bf7c0bf97d5df152c63c" commit_message="vb20: add vb2api_check_hash_get_digest() for retrieving hash result  For x86 systems, which resume through the boot reset vector, to implement vboot verification of the memory init code one needs check that the slot chosen on the resume path is the same as the original boot path. That check is done by storing the resulting hash of the slot. However, vb2api doesn't export the resulting hash from vb2api_check_hash(). Thus, provide a variant which saves the resulting digest in the supplied buffer.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46049 BRANCH=glados TEST=Suspended and resumed on chell. Also, tested with an EC build      which returns a bad hash to ensure that is properly caught.  Change-Id: Ic20be2024afedabc2d8bc767f1b794376348523c Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323460 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="323460" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/60/323460/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If2a814c90a941e6f46ab031909ce607d01a2c729" commit="9918d52f09e2f1f4a5388569e95b04e8f31c9286" commit_message="autotest: Read iw event log directly from host.  Currently, the IwEventLogger is only able to read the event log file after it has been copied to the autotest server after the event logger has been stopped. With this change, we will read the file directly from the host, to allow multiple checks within a single context, then copy it to the autotest server after we exit the context.  BUG=None TEST=Run jetstream sanity autotests which use the iw event logger.  Change-Id: If2a814c90a941e6f46ab031909ce607d01a2c729 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323771 Commit-Ready: Dane Pollock &lt;danepollock@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dane Pollock &lt;danepollock@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Filipe Brandenburger &lt;filbranden@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323771" owner_email="danepollock@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/71/323771/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaee7b1133a960f8cb2d8c9eae796445aa2d6e155" commit="86acb0e375c2260bf4d6053fbb797a280cf38518" commit_message="invocation: put dut_options into env instead of creating self.dut  In invocation.py dut_options is used for creating a dut object instead of set into env. This makes all dut.Create() in pytest generates wrong object. The CL fix this problem by setting env variable.  This CL also fixes a small bug in run_pytest, where usage of os.setenv and ast.dump is wrong.  BUG=None TEST=Run pytest with different dut options.  Change-Id: Iaee7b1133a960f8cb2d8c9eae796445aa2d6e155 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323930 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323930" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/30/323930/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3c6a3e97a3853b6ed9a46d354520ad75e8442b10" commit="bc58bddc4f11aaa8781aec8b131173d1980a2cea" commit_message="Build dev-util/bsdiff from AOSP.  bsdiff have seen some improvements in AOSP source based on the code we had in Chromium OS plus some extra changes in the AOSP side. More updates will come, so this CL switches the dev-util/bsdiff ebuild to build from AOSP.  List of new CLs included in this build. Not all of them important for Chromium OS.   f822e6c Fix reading extents file if not start from the beginning of a extent.   d87c835 Various fixes in bspatch and File class.   cdbad9a Build bspatch for the target.   cd1e453 Update NOTICE and LICENSE file.   792b0a5 Build unittests on Android.   437b7af bspatch: Re-enable extents support.   b870eb5 bspatch: Ran clang-format on bspatch.cc.   daf3516 FileInterface: Implement GetSize().   03f1deb bspatch: Use a C++ interface for file access.   20891f9 Convert C sources to C++.   e1526cf Ran clang-format on all the Chromium OS sources.   a09afd9 Merge &quot;Disable GNU extensions in bspatch code.&quot;   870b802 Disable GNU extensions in bspatch code.   b7e3b8e Update Android.mk to build Chromium OS changes.  BUG=chromium:580717 TEST=`emerge-link bsdiff` with and without cros_workon enabled.  Change-Id: I3c6a3e97a3853b6ed9a46d354520ad75e8442b10 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323383 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="323383" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/83/323383/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commi